<databaseChangeLog xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
                   xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
                   xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-4.1.xsd">
    <changeSet author="fineract" id="command-00008" context="postgresql,mysql">
        <comment>
            A repeated request is normally answered from the command's own result, which the web layer renders with
            the status it derived the first time, so nothing about the original response has to be recorded for it.
            This column covers the case that leaves no result behind - a failure, whose answer comes from an exception
            mapper, and an answer that is not JSON. There the recorded answer is thrown rather than returned, and
            nothing else could say what status to use.
        </comment>
        <addColumn tableName="m_command">
            <column name="response_status_code" type="int" />
        </addColumn>
    </changeSet>
</databaseChangeLog>
